    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3). `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the repo, and it covers the new E.164 behavior.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed telephone handling to store and compare numbers in **E.164** form.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 replaced the old \"strip to exactly 10 digits\" logic with a `toE164(...)` helper:\n- If the input has a leading `+`, the country code is kept as-is.\n- Otherwise `+61` is assumed and a single leading `0` is dropped from the national digits.\n- Spaces, dashes and brackets (all non-digits) are stripped.\n- The result must have 8\u201315 digits after the `+`, else a `400` (`InvalidOwnerFieldsException` naming `telephone`) is thrown.\n- `normalizeTelephone` (create) and the `updateOwner` path both now write back the E.164 string.\n- `rejectDuplicateTelephone` now compares E.164 values, converting each existing owner's stored number the same way (via `normalizeExisting`, which safely skips values that can't form valid E.164).\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 the `telephone` bean-validation constraint changed from `^[0-9]{10}$` (plus `@Digits`) to `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`, and the now-unused `@Digits` import was removed, so the entity accepts the E.164 string on persist.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `telephone` field description and example to document the E.164 normalization.\n\nVerified behavior matches the spec: `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678`, `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456`, and `12` is rejected with `400`.",
